 Growth, Lifts Core FFO to $0.48 and Adds $500M Buyback as It Sells Homes to Fund 6% Share Reduction","src":"BigGo Finance","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE9ic0VVVkhVenQ3akVnX1I1Zmh2X0JxX3E3SDN3dTlaamIxempnM3pzSkhZU0dGN2VNdmoxMmdNY3dQYkRPZ0FocXI3ZktDbmRKQjVmMXBzN0pxZjdwZlE?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"[Invitation Homes 2026 年第三季財報電話會議] Invitation Homes 混合租金成長 3%，將核心 FFO 提升至 0.48 美元，並因出售房屋為 6% 股份減少提供資金而增加 5 億美元回購"},{"title":"INVH Q3 FFO Meets Estimates, Revenues Miss, '26 Views Raised","src":"TradingView","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxNNVh4QkpVOVR1YXRoWEVyUWxEYTlJelZKdEJxVV9mc2s3UUpiX2JmZHlYVFRhOVFhRm1WcnFLQmhHLU5YOTF5eENYU01FOHIyYTcydERIZEw2dUNhWFlNMzdsdU14ODctUVdMMFVLUGZqUk1BY0FOS0NDVFB3NXZrSGI0YVVDT3J2elFPcnp2MW9ud0w4YmdwNjlvZ3JvVDlqUi1KMkdIOFR3aXdRSjl2YlJVVQ?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"INVH 第三季 FFO 達到預期，營收未達預期，'26 觀點提出"},{"title":"Invitation Homes Q3 AFFO Flat, Revenue Rises; Revises 2026 Guidance","src":"Yahoo Finance","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxQbHNtZTVDQ04wX0Zkc3MtSVFRVE11QWp3V293WjZDVUowUmJDOEZYWUxRVE5WMGRYNEp0WGVEenJyVF9YTFdLaTBQS0tsd0d4MTdaSEJnNE1mR1R3Z2dvWFlsYmhkZkxxZ0xzUlJSZTQ4b1h4a2VJWGZ3U0dac2h4V3JjOFI4Wm01WVVQTDBQOXlsN3I0UWc?oc=5","date":"2026-10-28","zh":"Invitation Homes 第三季 AFFO 持平，收入上升；修訂 2026 年指南"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":11},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":4}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-19","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1687229/000168722926000016/invh-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Invitation Homes is a leading owner and operator of single-family homes for lease, offering residents high-quality homes in sought-after neighborhoods across the United States. As of December 31, 2025, we wholly own 86,192 homes for lease, jointly own 8,006 homes for lease, and provide professional third-party property and asset management services for an additional 15,866 homes, all of which are primarily located in 16 core markets across the country. These homes help meet the needs of a growing share of Americans who count on the ease, flexibility, and savings of leasing. We provide our residents access to updated homes with features they value, as well as close proximity to jobs and good schools. The continued demand for our product proves that the choice and flexibility we offer are attractive to many people.","zh":null},{"en":"We operate in markets with strong demand drivers, high barriers to entry, and high rent growth potential, primarily in the Western United States, Florida, and the Southeast United States. Through disciplined market and asset selection, as well as through strategic mergers and acquisitions, we designed our wholly and jointly owned portfolios to capture the operating benefits of local density as well as economies of scale that we believe cannot be readily replicated. Since our founding in 2012, we have built a proven, vertically integrated operating platform that enables us to effectively and efficiently acquire, renovate, lease, maintain, and manage both the homes we own and those we manage on behalf of others.","zh":null},{"en":"The portfolio of homes we own average approximately 1,880 square feet with three to four bedrooms and two bathrooms, appealing to a resident base that we believe is less transitory than a typical multifamily resident. We invest in the upfront renovation of homes in our portfolio in order to address capital needs, reduce ongoing maintenance costs, and drive resident demand.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"We face competition from different sources in each of our primary activities: acquiring and leasing our properties and providing property and asset management services for single-family homes. We believe our competitors in acquiring or building homes for investment purposes are larger investors, including private equity funds and other REITs, that are seeking to capitalize on the same market opportunity that we have identified, and individual investors or small private investment partnerships, that are seeking investment properties that can either be leased or restored and sold. Our primary competitors in acquiring portfolios include large and small private equity investors, public and private REITs, and other sizable private institutional investors. These same competitors may also compete with us for residents and may provide property and asset management services similar to those that ","zh":null},{"en":"In addition, federal, state, and local regulatory developments, including executive actions and proposed federal and state legislation aimed at limiting institutional ownership and acquisition of single-family homes, may affect the competitive dynamics in our markets by imposing requirements or restrictions that apply differently to various categories of market participants. To the extent these developments disproportionately affect institutional owners, including us, or advantage other categories of investors, such as individual investors and smaller partnerships who may fall outside regulatory definitions, our ability to compete for acquisitions, residents, or capital on favorable terms could be adversely affected. See Part I. Item 1A. \"Risk Factors — Risks Related to Our Business and Operations — Executive actions and proposed federal and state legislation or regulations aimed at limi","zh":null}],"segments":{},"peers":["AMH","MAA","CPT","UDR","SUI"]}}